    {
      "id": 102,
      "title": "whitelisted-ngrok",
      "company": "Open Source",
      "role": "Creator & Maintainer",
      "description": "A Go CLI that wraps ngrok with an IP allowlist, so a local machine can be reachable from the internet without being open to everyone. Every inbound connection is checked against the whitelist before a single byte is forwarded - allowed addresses get a transparent bidirectional proxy, everything else is dropped at the door. Supports both TCP and HTTP endpoints, and can email you the tunnel URL the moment it comes up.",
